.env*
!.env.example
# .env.android holds ONE public value: VITE_API_BASE, the HTTPS URL of the
# deployed Render backend. It is compiled into the APK, so it can never hold a
# secret anyway -- and it must be committed, or a fresh clone builds an APK with
# an empty API base that fails every /api request. Keys stay in Render env vars.
!.env.android
